Package: iftop-json
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: bandwidth usage per connection on a network interface, as JSON
 iftop listens to network traffic on a named interface and works out the
 bandwidth used by each pair of hosts. This variant has no interactive
 display: every two seconds it writes the current statistics to standard
 output as one line of JSON, with the rates averaged over 2, 10 and 40
 seconds for every connection, plus the interface totals.
 .
 It is used by iftop-web, and can be installed next to the interactive iftop.

Package: iftop-web
Architecture: all
Depends:
 gunicorn,
 iftop-json (>= ${source:Version}),
 python3 (>= 3.11),
 python3-flask,
 python3-flask-limiter,
 python3-flask-login,
 python3-flaskext.wtf,
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: web interface showing live bandwidth usage per connection
 A web interface for iftop-json. A collector service runs iftop-json and keeps
 its latest output; a web service shows the connections with the most traffic
 as bars for sent and received data, updated every two seconds. Connections
 can be filtered, sorted by averaging window, and grouped by folding client
 ports.
 .
 All pages require a login. Users are managed with iftop-web-user. The web
 service listens on localhost by default; listening on other addresses
 requires TLS.
